cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below, and cite GEARS and the source datasets."
title: "perturbation-readouts: how much of a reported improvement is the choice of readout?"
abstract: >-
  A reproduction of GEARS on three public CRISPR perturbation datasets alongside
  a bipartite heterogeneous GNN, scoring both models with every readout this
  literature reports, on identical predictions and identical splits.
